<title>TAIWAN: Yangming strengthens Asia operations.</title>
<headline>Yangming strengthens Asia operations.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Yangming Marine Corp said on Friday it would strengthen its operations in Asia by cooperating with Taiwan's Cheng Lie Navagation Company to add a new weekly Japan-Taiwan-Hong Kong-Thailand route.</p>
<p>The two firms will use four 1,100 twenty-foot-equivalant-unit container ships to sail the new route from early November, a Yangming statement said.</p>
<p>&quot;The agreement will enhance our regional services,&quot; a Yangming executive said by telephone.</p>
<p>Yangming, one of Taiwan's biggest shipping firms, was privatised in February after an offer of 110 million shares, reducing its government stake to 48 percent from 56.5 percent.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
